  "notes": "Sheet 0 (FH2L Arquitectos, Casa VCH, Madrid): a long two-storey house in light travertine-like limestone in a wooded plot; a fully glazed ground floor set back under a limestone first-floor box that overhangs the pool terrace (photograph 1), the box faced in places by vertical timber louvres, big glazed bands and a thin roof slab; from the entry side a massive wall of large limestone blocks, a water channel leading to the foyer through a gravel garden of grasses and cacti (photographs 2 and 3), a skylit patio planted with a banana plant inside (photograph 5), a long pool to the south, the garden dropping away in terraces under pines and holm oaks (photograph 4). Modelled: the glazed ground floor, upper box and slab, timber louvres and windows, the entry wall and water channel, gravel garden, pool and terrace, retaining edge, trees. Guessed: dimensions (30 x 13 m footprint, 7.5 m high), the wing at the entry. A private home placed at its town only (Madrid)."
